9.693, 99.976], ["me", 99.976, 100.096], ["young", 100.096, 100.336], ["man", 100.336, 100.729], ["i", 100.946, 101.023], ["tell", 101.023, 101.228], ["him", 101.228, 101.305], ["my", 101.305, 101.425], ["name", 101.425, 101.716], ["every", 101.716, 101.887], ["morning", 101.887, 102.281], ["he", 102.471, 102.565], ["says", 102.565, 102.908], ["good", 103.13, 103.284], ["name", 103.284, 103.678], ["and", 103.94, 104.025], ["i", 104.025, 104.094], ["kept", 104.094, 104.359], ["everything", 104.359, 104.685], ["else", 104.685, 105.01], ["i", 105.222, 105.299], ["checked", 105.299, 105.719], ["i", 105.896, 105.982], ["write", 105.982, 106.179], ["it", 106.179, 106.256], ["all", 106.256, 106.427], ["down", 106.427, 106.752], ["just", 106.752, 106.966], ["in", 106.966, 107.052], ["case", 107.052, 107.429], ["my", 107.667, 107.804], ["diary", 107.804, 108.198], ["says", 108.198, 108.438], ["i", 108.438, 108.532], ["have", 108.532, 108.643], ["never", 108.643, 108.994], ["forgotten", 108.994, 109.422], ["a", 109.422, 109.465], ["thing", 109.465, 109.859], ["it", 110.153, 110.23], ["also", 110.23, 110.478], ["says", 110.478, 110.718], ["i", 110.718, 110.786], ["have", 110.786, 110.949], ["a", 110.949, 110.975], ["sister", 110.975, 111.497], ["there's", 111.733, 111.913], ["a", 111.913, 111.964], ["girl", 111.964, 112.366], ["at", 112.366, 112.426], ["our", 112.426, 112.538], ["table", 112.538, 112.949], ["every", 112.949, 113.248], ["morning", 113.248, 113.702], ["i've", 113.958, 114.053], ["been", 114.053, 114.207], ["calling", 114.207, 114.524], ["her", 114.524, 114.643], ["miss", 114.643, 115.2]], "lines": [[0.0, 7.99, "In this town, the tax is one memory a year, and the tax man gets to pick. My dad doesn't know my name anymore. On Thursday, it's my turn to pay."], [8.208, 12.992, "He puts two fingers on your forehead and reaches for the best thing in there. Whatever he touches, he keeps."], [13.271, 16.022, "Old Mr. Finch paid with his wedding. He's been a lot happier."], [16.261, 19.523, "The cook at the inn paid with her soup recipe. She's been guessing ever since."], [19.762, 24.791, "And the tax man keeps them. All of them. He's had four hundred first kisses, and none of them were his."], [25.092, 30.255, "Last year he took me, out of my dad. Dad's very polite to me now. He calls me \"young man.\""], [30.495, 33.087, "You start paying at ten. I turned ten on Sunday."], [33.384, 38.362, "My name is Ned, and I'm the kid who never forgets. Ask me what I had for lunch on any day of my life."], [38.611, 44.562, "So I've got a lot he'd like. My mom singing. The time it snowed in June. My dog, when he was small."], [44.85, 48.969, "On Monday, the tax man stopped at our gate and looked up at my window. He didn't knock."], [49.231, 57.636, "On Tuesday, I watched him do the widow next door, through her window. She was thinking about her cat. You could tell. He took the cat. She still feeds it. She doesn't know why."], [57.868, 61.012, "That's when I saw it. He doesn't dig. He takes whatever is on top."], [61.262, 70.805, "So on Wednesday night, I did not sleep. I picked one thing, and I wrote it in my diary, so I'd know what I lost. Then I sat up in bed and thought about it, as hard as I could, until morning."], [71.024, 74.303, "Thursday. He put two cold fingers on my forehead and smiled."], [74.586, 75.545, "Then he stopped smiling."], [75.803, 84.377, "There was only one thing on top. It was him. His fingers on my dad's head. His smile. And my dad's face, afterward, looking at me like I'd come to the wrong house."], [84.623, 86.52, "He had to take it. He'd already touched it."], [86.771, 88.578, "I don't think he had ever seen himself before."], [88.838, 95.474, "He walked out very slowly. At the door, he patted me on the head. Two fingers. A little too long. I thought that was strange."], [95.71, 99.06, "He hasn't collected since. They say he sits in his house with the curtains shut."], [99.231, 103.678, "Dad still calls me young man. I tell him my name every morning. He says, \"Good name.\""], [103.94, 107.429, "And I kept everything else. I checked. I write it all down, just in case."], [107.667, 109.859, "My diary says I have never forgotten a thing."], [110.153, 111.497, "It also says I have a sister."], [111.733, 115.2, "There's a girl at our table every morning. I've been calling her \"miss.\""]]}